# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets — .assetsignore (gitignore syntax, relative to the assets dir = dist)
# PERMANENT image architecture (no per-deploy file-count risk):
#   • Bulk content images (cm/ + hotels/ + food/ + gallery/) are EXCLUDED from the static bundle and served
#     from the R2 public bucket instead. Both the content layouts (Article/Roundup/ReviewLayout → asset())
#     AND the hub generator (gen-hubs → imgUrl()) prepend IMG_BASE = PUBLIC_IMG_BASE env
#     (default https://pub-65cf98dcb15e4c06a7a465ec411b870a.r2.dev), so every cm/hotels/food image URL points
#     at R2. Verified: 0 plain /images/(cm|hotels|food|gallery)/ refs remain in any generated HTML.
#   • heroes/ + cities/ STAY in the bundle (small, slow-growing): hub hero, neighbour cards and og:image use
#     plain /images/heroes|cities/ paths served straight from the deploy.
#
# File count: 22,627 total − hotels(7,693) − cm(3,216) − food(102) − gallery(1) ≈ 11,615 static files → well
# under Cloudflare's 20,000 limit, with ~8k headroom for growth. New content images just need to be in R2
# (see _internal/upload-r2*.{mjs,sh}); they never count against the bundle limit again.
images/hotels/
images/cm/
images/food/
images/gallery/
